The decisions demo: a Go module that keeps three MADR decision records under docs/decisions, beside a README that is no record. 0001 is an accepted MADR 2 record with its status and date in a list; 0002 is a MADR 4 record whose front matter scope governs src/payments; 0003 is a superseded record whose Scope section governs every Go file of a queue directory. The change edits src/payments/charge.go and src/billing/queue/worker.go and deletes 0001.
-- base/go.mod --
module github.com/acme/checkout

go 1.24
-- base/src/payments/charge.go --
package payments

// Charge charges an amount in cents.
func Charge(cents int) error {
	return nil
}
-- base/src/billing/queue/worker.go --
package queue

// Work drains the billing queue.
func Work() {}
-- base/docs/decisions/README.md --
# Decisions

The architecture decisions of the checkout, in MADR.
-- base/docs/decisions/0001-charges-are-synchronous.md --
# Charges are synchronous

* Status: accepted
* Date: 2025-02-10

## Context and Problem Statement

A charge either succeeds or fails before the checkout answers.

## Decision Outcome

Chosen option: charge synchronously.
-- base/docs/decisions/0002-payments-own-the-ledger.md --
---
status: accepted
date: 2025-03-04
decision-makers: payments team
scope:
  - src/payments/
---

# Payments own the ledger

## Context and Problem Statement

Only the payments package writes ledger entries.
-- base/docs/decisions/0003-one-queue-per-domain.md --
# One queue per domain

## Status

Superseded by [0002](0002-payments-own-the-ledger.md)

## Scope

- `src/**/queue/*.go`
- `docs/queues.md` (the queue map)

## Decision

Each domain drains its own queue.
-- head/src/payments/charge.go --
package payments

// Charge charges an amount in cents, and retries a declined charge once.
func Charge(cents int) error {
	if err := charge(cents); err != nil {
		return charge(cents)
	}
	return nil
}

func charge(cents int) error {
	return nil
}
-- head/src/billing/queue/worker.go --
package queue

// Work drains the billing queue until it is empty.
func Work() {
	for drain() {
	}
}

func drain() bool { return false }
-- delete/docs/decisions/0001-charges-are-synchronous.md --
